            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Septimius Severus</strong><br>\nSeptimius Severus was born in the city of Leptis Magna, located in the Roman province of Africa. Coming from a background of equestrian rank, Severus climbed the social ladder through military service. His early life prepared him for the challenges of Roman politics and military affairs. He showed great ambition and skill, which set the stage for his future ascendancy to the throne of Rome.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Power</strong><br>\nAfter the death of Emperor Pertinax, the empire was thrown into chaos, with various generals vying for power. Septimius Severus quickly seized the opportunity, declaring himself emperor in 193 AD. His claim was contested, but Severus defeated his rivals in a civil war that lasted until 197 AD. His victory in this conflict solidified his grip on the Roman Empire.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Military Campaigns</strong><br>\nSeverus was renowned for his military campaigns, which expanded the Roman Empire's boundaries. He strengthened the army by rewarding soldiers with pay raises and established a reputation as a formidable military leader. His campaigns in the East against the Parthian Empire were particularly celebrated, resulting in the annexation of new territories.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
