            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Governance and Administration</strong><br>\nDuring his rule, Severus implemented several administrative changes. He reformed the legal system and the structure of the Roman government to centralize power around the emperor. This included increasing the size and role of his personal bureaucracy and giving more power to his Praetorian Guard, the elite unit tasked with the emperor's security.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legal Reforms</strong><br>\nSeverus was also known for his contributions to Roman law. He allowed more equitable treatment for women and children in legal affairs and increased the access of provincials to the Roman courts. These reforms were in line with his philosophy of extending Roman citizenship rights and privileges to provincials.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural and Religious Influence</strong><br>\nHe promoted the Romanization of his African home province, which included the spread of the Latin language and Roman laws. Severus was tolerant of local religions as long as they did not conflict with Roman state interests. He was particularly supportive of the sun god Sol Invictus, who was increasingly popular in the Roman pantheon during his reign.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
