          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Building Projects</strong><br>\nSeverus was a great builder, leaving behind many monuments and structures across the empire. He enriched his hometown of Leptis Magna with splendid buildings and public works. His architectural legacy in Rome includes the famous Arch of Septimius Severus, which commemorates his victories in Parthia.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Family and Succession</strong><br>\nSeverus married Julia Domna, and they had two sons, Caracalla and Geta. He sought to secure a dynasty by naming them as successors. However, his plans for a peaceful succession would eventually fail, as his sons became bitter rivals, leading to turmoil after his death.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nSeptimius Severus died in 211 AD while in Britain, ending his nearly two-decade rule over the Roman Empire. His death marked the end of a stable period for the empire. Despite his efforts to create a lasting dynasty, the years following his death were marked by instability and conflict, highlighting the complexity of Severus's legacy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
